WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.589
Imagine you are walking down the street to
do some shopping and suddenly a roof tile

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:07.920
lands on your head.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.809
"What is that supposed to mean?"

00:00:10.809 --> 00:00:18.990
you ask yourself and you go inside the department
store from which the tile fell off to complain.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.820
The owner of the department store shows little
interest in your misfortune and says that

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.420
he cannot explain how it happened.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.900
Of course, you also have no idea how exactly
the tile landed on your head – but because

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:41.219
you have a concussion, you go to a lawyer
and sue in court.

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:45.720
What happens next depends on whether the incident
happened in a country that practices Civil

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.219
Law or one that applies Common Law.

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:57.460
Do you know which of the two is practiced
where you live?

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.309
Let's say the whole thing happens to you in
Germany, which belongs to the Continental

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:06.250
European Legal System, where Civil Law applies.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.970
How does the judge evaluate your case?

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.700
She is looking for a legal provision that
fits your case.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:20.659
In the German Civil Code, article 838, she
will find the general rule that a building

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:25.340
user has to maintain the structure and is
responsible for the damage caused if parts

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.920
of the building break off.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.049
The judge then examines the law.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.939
She checks if the defendant really is the
user of the building, if he has to maintain

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:40.689
the building by law, and whether he had negligently
failed to do so.

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:46.590
If all those legal elements are fulfilled,
the department store operator is liable, and

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:51.399
you, as the plaintiff who instituted the legal
proceedings, will receive compensation for

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:55.570
the suffering caused by the event.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:02:00.420
If you had taken your walk in the United States,
which belongs to the Anglo-American Legal

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:06.250
System, the Common Law, the judge would proceed
differently.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:11.650
In the US, the judge would instead look for
a comparable case – such as the English

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:17.750
case of Byrne v. Boadle from 1863, in which
pretty much the same thing had happened to

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:25.810
a poor passerby, only it had not been a loose
brick, but rather a barrel stored in the building.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:31.060
In this case, the court held the department
store owner responsible, even though the plaintiff

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.590
could not prove negligence on the part of
the defendant.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:40.850
So what are the differences between Civil
Law and Common Law?

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:48.060
The legal systems are differentiated primarily
on the basis of their way of thinking!

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:53.450
The Civil Law System is characterized by thinking
on the basis of general and abstract legal

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:59.060
provisions, most of which are laid down in
codifications - such as the Civil Code in

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:05.310
Germany.The judge works deductively by applying
the general rule to the concrete case - a

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:10.519
technique known as subsumption.

00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:15.260
The Common Law System is characterized by
similar cases that happened in the past.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:21.230
The so-called doctrine of stare decisis, Latin
for “to stand by things decided”, binds

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:25.319
judges to precedents — cases that happened
in the past.

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:30.870
That is why the judge works on a case-by-case
basis and compares them with one another.If

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:35.730
the judge wants to deviate from a previous
decision, the so-called “Distinguishing”

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:41.110
is used to determine the differences between
the case at hand and the precedent.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:48.950
In summary, to determine wrongdoing and compensation,
the civil law system relies on the code of

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:54.560
law interpreted by judges, while the common
law system relies on similar cases from the

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.560
past.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:56.920
What are your thoughts?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.040
Which legal system is better?

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.260
Share your thoughts in the comments below
and tell us what type of law is practiced

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:24.330
in the country you are from.

